<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Hardie targets A$20 mln EBIT in Asia.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Hardie targets A$20 mln EBIT in Asia.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian building materials group James Hardie Industries Ltd said on Wednesday it has targetted earnings before interest and tax (EBIT) of A$20 million in the next three years from its Asian operations.</p>
<p>James Hardie executive general manager international, Ken Boundy, told a briefing that the group was looking to expand into Asia in four areas.</p>
<p>- Residential recladding in Japan.</p>
<p>- Through a fibre cement joint venture in the Philippines.  </p>
<p>- Developing building facade systems for Singapore, Malaysia, Indonesia and South Korea and developing housing construction systems for Indonesia, Philippines and Malaysia.</p>
